(A circle is symmetric across 8 octants. By calculating points in the first octant where 0 <= x <= y, we can plot 8 symmetric points: \(a+x, b+y\), \(a-x,) Tj
T* (b+y\), \(a+x, b-y\), \(a-x, b-y\), \(a+y, b+x\), \(a-y, b+x\), \(a+y, b-x\), \(a-y, b-x\). The initial decision parameter is p = 1 - r. If p < 0, next point is \(x+1, y\) and p =) Tj
T* (p + 2*x + 1; else next point is \(x+1, y-1\) and p = p + 2*\(x - y\) + 1.) Tj
