(An ellipse with semi-major axis rx and semi-minor axis ry has equation ry²x² + rx²y² - rx²ry² = 0. The curve is divided into two regions based on) Tj
T* (slope dy/dx = -1 \(where 2*ry²*x = 2*rx²*y\). In Region 1, x increments by 1 with decision parameter p1. In Region 2, y decrements by 1 with decision) Tj
T* (parameter p2.) Tj
