(2D affine transformations modify the position, orientation, or size of geometric shapes. Translation shifts vertices by \(tx, ty\). Rotation spins points) Tj
T* (around the triangle center \(cx, cy\) by an angle theta. Scaling expands or shrinks points relative to centroid by \(sx, sy\). Reflection mirrors coordinates) Tj
T* (across the horizontal center line y = cy via ny = 2*cy - y. Shearing slants points along the X-axis via nx = x + shx*\(y - cy\).) Tj
