(The Cohen-Sutherland algorithm divides the 2D plane into 9 regions using 4-bit outcodes \(Top, Bottom, Right, Left: TBRL\). Region codes: INSIDE =) Tj
T* (0000, LEFT = 0001, RIGHT = 0010, BOTTOM = 0100, TOP = 1000. Lines are classified: 1\) Trivial Accept: both endpoints outcodes are 0000 \(code1) Tj
T* (| code2 == 0\). 2\) Trivial Reject: bitwise AND is non-zero \(code1 & code2 != 0\). 3\) Clipping: compute intersection with boundary line using parametric) Tj
T* (slope equations.) Tj
