(A 3D cube is represented by 8 vertices \(x, y, z\). To display it on a 2D screen, oblique parallel projection is used: px = x + z/2, py = y - z/2. 3D) Tj
T* (Translation shifts all vertices: x' = x + tx, y' = y + ty, z' = z + tz. 3D Rotation about the Z-axis leaves z unaffected while rotating \(x, y\) around the cube) Tj
T* (center: x' = cx + \(x-cx\)*cos\(theta\) - \(y-cy\)*sin\(theta\), y' = cy + \(x-cx\)*sin\(theta\) + \(y-cy\)*cos\(theta\). 3D Scaling multiplies offsets by scale factors \(sx,) Tj
T* (sy, sz\).) Tj
